{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the people heard this evil thing.</b> What is it? It is the verse after it, \"And YHWH said to Moses, say to the children of Israel\" (Exodus 33:5). And like it, \"And YHWH said to Moses in Midian\" (above, Exodus 4:19), which I have already explained. \"Can he even give bread?\" (Psalms 78:20) — for like it is \"And He commanded the skies above\" (there, v. 23), and He had already commanded the skies, and thus this one, and there is no need for the emendation of the Gaon [Saadia], who did thus always:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The Hebrew of the last phrase is textually difficult; read hyper-literally as rendered. The reference to 'the Gaon's emendation' likely concerns a reading of the grammatical form ויאמר as pluperfect, consistent with the examples cited."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:02.623631229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}